---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Different Minds. New Ways to Work."
  description="A personal reflection on AI agents, neurodivergence, and the possibility of new ways to work together."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">NEURODIVERGENT / MY COMMITMENT</p>
      <h1>Different minds.<br /><em>New ways to work.</em></h1>
      <p>
        AI is changing my sense of what I can do. It makes me wonder what that
        could mean for the ways we work together.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="narrative">
      <p>
        The way I see it, the journey from agricultural to industrial society
        has largely been a story of organizing people at scale. Shared
        schedules, standardized roles, and predictable routines made
        coordination possible, while setting a narrow default for how people
        should pay attention, communicate, and contribute.
      </p>
      <p>
        That default largely reflects neurotypical expectations. For minds that
        work differently, fitting into the organization can consume energy that
        could otherwise go into discovery and creation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working with AI agents has made more of my ideas feel within reach. That
        experience makes me hopeful about what AI could mean for neurodivergent
        people, including those with ADHD, autism, and other forms of
        neurodivergence: more room to work with our strengths and give our ideas
        a life beyond our heads.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m committed to exploring new organizational structures and ways of
        collaborating, with AI and neurodivergent ways of thinking built into
        their foundations—so our potential has room to develop fully.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="vision-quote">
      <blockquote>
        “be more of an artist, look at things from a different direction, be
        able to build something unique.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        Alex Karp, Palantir CEO, on different ways of thinking in the AI era
        <a
          href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/full-interview-alex-karp-on-ai-job-loss-and-the-future-of-work/id1772360235?i=1000754930232"
          >TBPN · Original interview · March 12, 2026 ↗</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://fortune.com/2026/03/24/palantir-ceo-alex-karp-two-people-successful-in-ai-era-vocational-skills-neurodivergence-gen-z-career-advice/"
          >Read the coverage in Fortune ↗</a
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Site>

<style>
  .narrative {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .narrative p + p {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .vision-quote {
    margin-block: 48px 64px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
    background: var(--wash);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    max-width: 850px;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--primary);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  figcaption a {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
</style>
